# JavaScript

Vanilla ES modules — no bundler, no framework. Match existing files.

## Module boundaries

| Module | Responsibility |
|--------|----------------|
| `config.js` | Default watchlist seed + tunable constants + optional `CARTO_BASEMAP_API_KEY` |
| `watchlist.js` | localStorage load/save/add/remove for watchlist |
| `api.js` | data.gov.hk fetch, format, metadata caches, coalesced/bounded ETA requests with sequence-aware caches; `ensureStopsIndex`, `fetchStopRoutes` |
| `cache.js` | localStorage read/write with TTL |
| `estimate.js` | Bus position math, polyline helpers |
| `positionSmoothing.js` | Per-route display continuity across ETA revisions (`createPositionSmoother`) |
| `routing.js` | Ordered OSRM leg geometry + stop boundary indices, overlapping chunks, validated route cache |
| `map.js` | Full-bleed Leaflet map, tile-provider selection, idle GPS follow, focus overlays, add-pick mode, active-area fit |
| `pulse.js` | Nerve pulse renderer: track + uniform dash stream on current leg (`createPulseController`) |
| `geo.js` | Geolocation watch + listeners |
| `theme.js` | Light/dark + HK solar schedule |
| `refreshScheduler.js` | Per-entry ETA polling deadlines: focused 12 s, other entries 60 s; in-flight coalescing and visibility lifecycle |
| `app.js` | DOM orchestration only — no API URLs here |

## Naming

- `camelCase` functions and variables
- `UPPER_SNAKE` for exported config constants
- Watchlist entries: `id`, `route`, `stopId`, `direction`, `label`

## Patterns

- `async/await` for I/O; use `readCache`/`writeCache` for localStorage
- In-memory `Map` for session caches (`api.js`, `routing.js`)
- Tunables go in `config.js`, not scattered in feature modules
- Basemap provider selection belongs in `map.js`: `CARTO_BASEMAP_API_KEY` is configured in the checked-in defaults, selecting CARTO `light_all` / `dark_all` with a URL-encoded `key` parameter; an empty key uses standard OpenStreetMap raster tiles (`maxNativeZoom: 19`, `maxZoom: 20`). Use matching provider attribution. The OSM tile layer gets `.map-tiles--osm` for its dark-mode filter; keep overlays outside that filter.
- DOM: build elements in JS (`createRowElement`), `data-id` on rows, delegate on `#cards`
- Focus/map async: cancel stale work with `focusToken` + `selectionKey()` pattern. Full focus refreshes also increment `focusRefreshGeneration`; only the latest requested generation may commit. Initial and full geometry work must also match each entry's current `api.etaModelKey()` before committing, retrying against the latest source when it changed. The key includes the source snapshot plus first/second arrival ETA, sequence, direction, and destination, but excludes receive time and generated-at metadata; an identical 12 s observation must not invalidate pending geometry. `commitEntryResult()` is the shared selection/poll commit path: an older receive observation cannot overwrite a newer stored one, and transport errors paint the row error while retaining the last successful source until ETA expiry. These guards do not change the wall-time tracking clock.
- Map stage: `initMapStage` mounts Leaflet on boot; idle mode uses `followYouInActiveArea` (Maps/Uber-style: always move you marker; recenter into top half via single animated `setView` with projected south offset only when you leave the soft `IDLE_FOLLOW_WINDOW` around the top-half center, or on first fix / `force`); focus mode uses `activeAreaPadding` (~50% bottom inset, extra top for stop labels) in `fitBounds` / `scheduleFitToMarkers` so you + stop(s) + bus(es) frame above the watch-sheet; boarding pins use `stopIcon({ selected, label: nameEn, colorIndex })` for a glass name tooltip (deduped by stop id across multi-focus; first comma splits onto a secondary line); any number of routes may be focused (colors cycle 6-entry `ROUTE_COLORS`); you marker stays visible whenever GPS is available; `syncDockButton` sets `#add-route-btn` to `nav-dock__add--clear` when add-flow is active (`isAddFlowActive`) or `ids.length > 1` (multi-focus click → `exitFocus`; add-flow click → `cancelAddFlow`); single focus keeps **+**; `hideFocusPanel` clears route overlays and resumes idle follow (map never unmounts); `isFocusPanelVisible` means route focus is active, not that the map exists
- Watchlist rows: iOS-style swipe-to-delete via `--row-swipe-x` on `.row__slide` (axis-locked vs list scroll); `row__delete` confirms remove; no long-press edit mode
- Focus estimate merge: `loadEstimateForEntry` preserves `boardingStop.nameEn` when the estimate object omits it
- Focus map viewport: `scheduleFitToMarkers` (double rAF after `invalidateSize`) frames stop + bus + approach pulse + you on select; also when the nerve pulse, bus marker, or you marker first appears
- Tracking time: `api.trackingNowMs()` returns current device wall time for absolute ETAs. Source `snapshotMs` is freshness metadata, never a clock offset or a polling deadline. Keep actual `receivedAtMs` metadata on lightweight and full updates, including repeated snapshots. `resolveActiveBoardingEta` hands off to `second` once `first` expires against wall time.
- Ordered route geometry: `roadSnapRoute(stops)` returns `{ points, stopIndices }`, with one boundary index per input stop occurrence. OSRM requests use unsimplified `steps=true` / `geometries=geojson` leg geometry and validate each leg against its snapped waypoint endpoints with a bounded 2 m tolerance for OSRM endpoint discrepancies; retain the actual ordered step geometry and require exact continuity between steps. Retain all waypoints through overlapping chunks of at most 25 stops; deduplicate only adjacent identical points so loop revisits remain distinct. The `bus:osrm:v3` cache stores this metadata for seven days; do not reuse old point-only entries. Failed or malformed chunks use ordered stop-to-stop fallback without caching it. Points-only routing wrappers delegate to the same implementation. Build the full estimate polyline once, then derive the approach as its prefix at the boarding boundary; do not use global nearest-point searches or waypoint thinning to map stops onto the route.
- Stop occurrence identity: maps, upstream sampling, and ETA-chain points use canonical route-stop `seq` so repeated stop IDs remain distinct. A physical stop ID appearing once in the selected direction is unambiguous regardless of missing or different API ETA sequence numbers. Resolve its coordinate index by ID + canonical sequence after any coordinate failures, never by the original route-array index. A nonpositive approach distance produces no bus placement or pulse; do not fabricate a boarding position when upstream geometry is unavailable or all resolved stops coincide. The watchlist still stores no occurrence sequence. OSRM's driving profile and ETA matching do not supply bus GPS positions or vehicle identity.
- ETA sequence calibration: Citybus ETA `seq` and route-stop `seq` can have different origins. `inferEtaSequenceOffset()` requires at least two distinct unique-stop anchors and agreement across every valid API sequence in their collected observations; verify a zero offset too. Unique selected upstream stops are fetched without a sequence filter. A unique boarding stop can be an anchor, and up to two additional unique route stops may be requested when the selected unique request set is insufficient; calibration-only extras do not enter the position chain. Repeated boarding maps `active.seq - offset` to its canonical visit only after calibration. Missing, conflicting, or uncalibrated repeated boarding returns `ambiguous-stop` with full-route/physical-pin context and no bus or pulse; never fall back to the first visit or match raw sequence equality. Unresolved repeated upstream stops remain unknown. `boardingStop.apiSeq` retains the raw API sequence for lightweight occurrence-change checks; do not compare incoming API sequences with canonical geometry sequences. Normalize API sequences to positive integers or unknown; changed values, including known/unknown transitions, require full re-estimation.
- ETA chains: `matchBusEta` still chooses the earliest upstream ETA that is travel-time plausible against boarding (`dist / Δt ≤ MAX_BUS_SPEED_M_PER_MIN`). `buildEtaChain` anchors boarding last and calls `sanitizeEtaChain`, which keeps the longest plausible subsequence in route order: finite nonnegative cumulative distances, strictly increasing distances/times, every adjacent leg ≤ `MAX_BUS_SPEED_M_PER_MIN` (600 m/min). Slow legs are valid; ties prefer downstream points. Revalidate after lightweight boarding ETA changes. Candidate association remains heuristic.
- Missing upstream ETAs: absent, empty, remark-only, failed, or rejected matches provide no passage evidence. Do not advance a minimum position from them; production estimates use the route origin as the lower bound. Progress comes from validated matched ETAs, with speed fallback when no usable chain remains. Missing data supplies no vehicle identity or passage history.
- Shared placement: `resolveBusPlacement()` uses validated chain interpolation when at least two points remain; speed fallback is used otherwise. Before the first credible future stop, raw extrapolation stays upstream of it. Do not reintroduce a second boarding-countdown position or mutable closing-speed state. Both `routesFromEstimates()` and `applyBusAndPulseToMap()` use the position smoother's displayed placement for the bus and pass that same value to `resolveApproachPulse()`; pulse bounds use physical stop distances around that placement, even when intermediate ETAs are missing. Leg intervals are half-open so an exact stop boundary selects the next leg. Tracking and upstream ETA fetching continue through the final minute; keep the marker on the predicted road path without an ETA-threshold snap to raw stop coordinates. Expiry and handoff still use the boarding ETA against wall time.
- Position smoothing: `positionSmoothing.createPositionSmoother()` keeps presentation state per focused route. Rebase a meaningful ETA revision from the current displayed cumulative distance, then decay the residual with smoothstep over `BUS_POSITION_BLEND_MS` (5 s) while the raw model continues moving. Interpolate along the ordered polyline, stay within route bounds, and converge exactly at completion; backward corrections are allowed. A cloned but identical position model or metadata-only update must not restart a transition. Compare ordered geometry, physical stop boundaries, and canonical/raw boarding occurrence identity once per revision; never project a previous latitude/longitude onto a loop.
- Smoothing lifecycle: use monotonic `performance`/rAF time for correction progress and wall time for ETA expiry. Reset on unavailable placement, expired previous boarding ETA, detected handoff, changed occurrence/geometry, an ETA revision of at least `BUS_POSITION_MAX_ETA_SHIFT_MS` (5 min), deselection, or hidden/resumed document. Consume handoff evidence before clearing it. Lightweight updates replace estimates and chain points instead of mutating the smoother's previous model. Clear stale state before resuming so background time does not produce a catch-up animation. Presentation smoothing changes no ETA chains, passage constraints, or vehicle identity assumptions.
- Pulse rendering: `slicePolylineBetween()` extracts the physical current leg; `map.updateBusMarker()` paints the route-colored bus divIcon. `pulse.createPulseController()` owns the pearl track and uniform rounded-dash stream through the map geometry/motion wrappers. Pass actual remaining metres from the shared bus placement to interpolate each dash's geometric length from 18 px at ≥300 m to 3 px at ≤20 m, and its visible gap from 10 px to 3 px. Zoom-scale both, clamp the clear gap to at least 1.5 px, and include the fixed 3.5 px round-cap stroke width in pitch and bounds. All dashes and internal gaps are equal within a frame; no taper. Extend the final SVG gap beyond the path plus spacing/cap allowance so no repeated pattern appears behind the bus. Advance phase by constant pixel speed (28 px/s at reference zoom), preserving phase within one spacing as lengths, gaps, or styling change; dashes enter at the bus and exit at the stop without a whole-trail wrap or fade. Full ETA overlay repaints must retain controller layers and phase for routes with active legs; clear dropped/unavailable streams and reset phase for changed physical geometry. Repaint passes authoritative `remainingM` with `dtMs: 0`, so painting adds no animation time. Use actual map zoom for measurement invalidation even when visual scaling is clamped, and `noClip: true` for both pulse polylines so panning cannot change dash geometry. Check the actual SVG `d` path each frame and refresh metrics only on geometry/zoom/path changes, including delayed Leaflet reprojection after auto-fit or pinch zoom; stable frames must not call `getTotalLength()`. Reduced motion keeps the same stream stationary. `fadeOutActiveSegment` clears the pulse on handoff. These renderer rules do not alter estimated bus placement or physical leg bounds. Focus mode passes `denseUpstream: true`.
- Focus refresh tiers: `refreshEntries(ids)` loads and paints only the due watchlist entries. Evaluate successful received focused results only; an unchecked focused entry is not a missing response. Changed source snapshot, active boarding ETA time/API sequence, `FOCUS_REFRESH_INTERVAL_MS` (60 s), animation ETA expiry, or handoff triggers full upstream re-estimation for selected routes. Otherwise `applyLightweightFocusEtaUpdate()` updates boarding ETA/fetch metadata and revalidates the chain without repeated upstream fetches every 12 s. Failed checks retain the displayed estimate until its boarding ETA expires. rAF calls `applyBusAndPulseToMap()` with the shared displayed placement; on cleared ETA, fade the pulse and clear the marker.
- Watchlist refresh: `refreshScheduler.createRefreshScheduler({ getEntryIds, getFocusedIds, onRefresh, isActive, onCountdown })` owns fixed per-entry request-start deadlines: `FOCUSED_ETA_REFRESH_INTERVAL_MS` (12 s) for all focused IDs and `WATCHLIST_REFRESH_INTERVAL_MS` (60 s) for the others. No sentinel, snapshot phase-lock, or learned publication period. Group due IDs into selective refresh batches; coalesce in-flight requests for the same ID while allowing disjoint due entries to proceed. `notifyEntriesChanged()` checks new/promoted entries immediately, returns demoted entries to a minute from their last check, and preserves unrelated deadlines. `refreshNow()` checks all current entries and joins existing in-flight work; pause/resume follows document visibility, with immediate checks on resume. Async completion must not restart paused timers or revive removed entries; overdue work performs one current check rather than replaying missed ticks. Countdown is the earliest next deadline, or `refreshing` while requests run.
- ETA request lifetime: `ETA_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS` (8 s) covers fetch and response-body parsing. Coalesce only the raw payload for concurrent requests to the same physical route + stop; direction/occurrence filtering and sequence-aware caches remain independent. A timed-out request reports `ETA request timed out` and keeps the entry's normal polling tier; it must not teach a slower publication cadence. Browser timer throttling and network completion time are not guarantees of exact response timing. Selective checks label a focused-only partial batch `Checked focused HH:mm`; other batches use `Checked HH:mm`.
- Upstream ETAs: fetch unique physical stop IDs without `stopSeq`; fetch repeated visits with `{ stopSeq: canonicalSeq + verifiedOffset }`. This filter applies to raw API ETA `seq` before selecting arrivals, and the in-memory cache key includes that raw sequence (`all` for an unfiltered request). Use `{ useCache: true, cacheTtlMs: UPSTREAM_ETA_CACHE_TTL_MS }` unless `refreshUpstream`. Keep canonical route-stop `seq`, raw API ETA `seq`, arrival-order `eta_seq`, and vehicle identity distinct.
- Add-flow (`.add-anchor` above watch-sheet): **+** opens `add-menu` — full-screen `.add-menu-backdrop` blur + two `.add-menu__choice` glass bubbles (**Find nearby** / **Enter manually**) stacked above `#add-route-btn`; `openAddMenu` / `closeAddMenu({ immediate })`; **+** → **×** while menu or flow active (`body.add-menu-open`, `syncDockButton`); nearby: `startNearbyFlow` → `ensureStopsIndex()` → filter `NEARBY_STOP_RADIUS_M` → `enterAddPickMode({ instantSelect: true })` → `fetchStopRoutes` → `.add-flow__route-list`; manual: `startManualFlow` → route typeahead → direction → map pick + **✓**; `addState.step` includes `nearby-loading` | `nearby-picking` | `stop-routes` | `route` | `direction` | `picking`; cancel stale loads with `loadToken`; `body.add-flow-active` blocks `#cards`; focus and add-pick mutually exclusive
- Swallow errors only at prefetch/UI boundaries; `console.warn` for focus/estimate failures

## Adding code

Extend the owning module. Do not add dependencies or a build step.

## When shipping JS changes

Update this file if you add a module, shift responsibilities, or introduce a new pattern. Also update `docs/PRD.md` per [workflow.mdc](workflow.mdc) — same turn, no prompt needed.
